<title>MAURITIUS: Mauritius surveying sugar cane after cyclone.</title>
<headline>Mauritius surveying sugar cane after cyclone.</headline>
<dateline>PORT LOUIS 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Mauritius Chamber of Agriculture on Monday gathered data on possible damage to sugarcane fields from tropical cyclone Daniella, which passed near the Indian Ocean island on Sunday.</p>
<p>&quot;Data are still being collected. We would prefer to have all of them before making the assessment,&quot; Axel Pellegrin, senior assistant secretary at the chamber, told Reuters.</p>
<p>Pellegrin added he expected the survey to be completed on Tuesday afternoon.</p>
</text>
